  "id": "DrugBank_DB00047 - MONDO_5015",
  "verbalization": "Insulin Glargine, a long-acting insulin analog, is linked to Diabetes Mellitus (disease) through a series of indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Insulin Glargine is associated with Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus, which in turn is linked to other drugs like Albiglutide and Voglibose. These connections imply that Insulin Glargine may influence glucose metabolism, potentially through its role in insulin secretion or action, which is a key mechanism in the development of diabetes. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible dependency on insulin-like effects, which could be a critical factor in the pathophysiology of diabetes. The evidence supports a mechanism where Insulin Glargine may contribute to the regulation of blood glucose levels, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
